<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.itstomsh.yamep.lite</id>
  <name>Yamep Lite</name>
  <summary>Lightweight Markdown editor with a live preview</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>GPL-3.0-or-later</project_license>
  <developer id="io.github.itstomsh">
    <name>tomsh</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>Yamep Lite is the small variant of Yamep: the same editor and file tree, with the preview rendered by Qt itself instead of a browser engine. Notes are plain Markdown files in a folder you choose.</p>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Preview without an embedded browser engine</li>
      <li>Toolbar for headings, lists, tables, code, links and task lists</li>
      <li>File tree for the folder you are working in</li>
      <li>Atomic saves, and a prompt when a note is changed on disk by another program</li>
      <li>Light, dark and blue themes</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
